at commit e74f2c6bd4422bd1e12d257d1725bcce1d6b9ddd:

- prompts/*.md and prompts/tools.json are copied unmodified from
  internal/config/template/prompts/ and internal/config/toolsconfig/tools.json.
- native.py embeds, verbatim, OCR's review-filter tool definitions (internal/agent/agent.go:
  filterTools), its tool "side" wording (internal/config/toolsconfig/comparison.go) and its
  final-round message (internal/reviewtask/task.go).
- native.py is a Python port of OCR's deterministic review code: diff loading and parsing
  (internal/diff/git.go, parser.go, quotedpath.go), grouping (internal/agent/grouping.go),
  prompt assembly and round bookkeeping (internal/agent/agent.go, util.go), comment
  positioning and re-location (internal/diff/resolver.go, relocation.go), and comment
  normalisation (internal/tool/code_comment.go).

Changes relative to Open Code Review's native mode: model calls are made by Claude Code
subagents instead of an API provider, and a <harness> block maps OCR's tools onto Claude
Code's tools. README.md, "What differs from OCR's native mode", lists every other difference.

